DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T133000
SUMMARY:Let's Learn GitHub Copilot SDK (Java)
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nJoin this beginner-friendly livestr
 eam to learn how to build agentic applications with the GitHub Copilot SDK
  for Java\, without implementing the agent loop yourself. Unlike calling a
  model API directly\, the SDK gives your application programmatic access t
 o Copilot’s agent runtime\, including conversation management\, planning
 \, tool orchestration\, streaming events\, and session state. During the s
 ession\, we’ll explore clients\, sessions\, prompts\, and the agent runt
 ime. You’ll learn how to create multi-turn conversations\, stream respon
 ses in real time\, expose application functions as tools\, connect externa
 l capabilities through MCP servers\, and control agent behavior with hooks
  and permission handlers. We’ll also help you understand when to use the
  Copilot SDK instead of the interactive Copilot CLI: use the CLI for devel
 oper tasks in the terminal\, and use the SDK when you want to embed Copilo
 t’s agentic capabilities in your own application or service. No prior ex
 perience with the GitHub Copilot SDK is required.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3163
 15106/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260828T174946Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260828T174946Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315415338@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045639Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T170000
SUMMARY:When One Agent Isn't Enough: Orchestrating Secure Parallel Agent S
 warms
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nAI agents need to run code\, call A
 PIs\, and fan out in parallel - but doing that safely at scale is hard.\n\
 nThis session shows how to build agentic workloads on hardware-isolated\, 
 sub-second\, disposable compute that agents can provision themselves. Watc
 h a live research-agent swarm spin up a fleet of secure sandboxes in paral
 lel\, run real work in true isolation\, and tear it down automatically - w
 ith keyless auth throughout.\n\nPowered by Azure Container Apps Sandboxes.
  You'll learn\n• Why untrusted agent code and multi-agent fan-out break 
 traditional container/VM approaches\n• The pattern for safe\, ephemeral\
 , per-agent compute: isolation\, instant start\, scale-to-zero\, snapshot/
 resume\n• How agents can self-provision compute as a tool to extend thei
 r own capabilities\n• Controlling blast radius with hardware isolation\,
  egress policies\, and keyless managed identity\n• A working orchestrati
 on pattern for parallel agent swarms you can adapt to your own workloads\n
 \n[Explore the Build Cloud Native Apps series](https://developer.microsoft
 .com/reactor/series/S-1692?wt.mc_id=meetup_27397_webpage_reactor)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3154
 15338/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260625T180616Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260625T180616Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
